                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span>Under the general direction of the Chief Psychiatrist, Correctional Facility (Safety) of Integrated Gender Affirming Healthcare Program (IGAHP), in the Statewide Mental Health Program (SMHP), the Senior Psychiatrist, Correctional Facility (Specialist) serves as a statewide subject matter (SME) expert in gender-affirming mental health (MH) care who will have psychiatric clinical responsibilities, contribute to quality management, participate in the education of other staff members, and serve as a cross-discipline liaison and collaborator to assist institutions in delivering optimized gender-affirming health care within IGAHP. The Senior Psychiatrist, Specialist will also author, review, and consult on Transgender, Respect, Agency, and Digniaty Act (TRADA) MH evaluations for gender-based housing requests, MH gender-affirming surgery (GAS) evaluations, and Gender Dysphoria evaluations. The Senior Psychiatrist, specialist will work closely with Psychiatry, Psychology, Clinical Social Work, Nursing, Medical, Administrative, Custody (including PREA staff, DAI/FOPS), and Supervisory/Managerial colleagues as an integral member to develop solutions to complex problems involving gender-affirming care. for the transgender and gender diverse (TGD) population within CDCR. </span><span style="font-weight: bold;">Statewide travel and travel into correctional facilities is required.</span></span></p><p style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-weight: bold;"><br /></span></span></p><p style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-weight: bold;">IMPORTANT</span><span>: Please follow the link to share how you learned about this job opportunity with CCHCS.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">Link to Survey: </span><span style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 12pt;"><a href="https://cdcrca.sjc1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_db45Bxa32f8YGJE" style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; text-decoration: none;"><span style="color: #0000ff; font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline;">Click Here</span></a></span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;"><br />This position is located in the Mental Health Program. &nbsp;The program’s mission is to provide ethical, professional, and effective mental health care services for patients within all 35 of California Department of Corrections and Rehabilitation’s institutions statewide. With a competent, well-trained staff, they are committed to providing optimal care, promoting patients’ successful reintegration into society, and reducing recidivism.<br /><br /></span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 4pt 0pt 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">This advertisement is for a Senior Psychiatrist (Specialist), CR&amp;S&nbsp;position(s) located at HQ&nbsp;in Elk Grove, Sacramento County. Please indicate the position number on your application: 065-923-9759-013.<br /><br /></span></p><p style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 4pt 0pt 0pt;"><span style="font-weight: bold;">Note:</span><span> Main communication for this position will be through email. &nbsp;Please ensure you have a valid email address on your application.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 4pt 0pt 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;"> </span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;"><span style="font-weight: bold;"><br />Please note:</span><span> A Training and Development (T&amp;D) assignment will not be considered at this time</span></span><span>.<br /> </span></span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;"><br />This is a limited term position which may be extended or become permanent.</span></span></p><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=25910338&name=065-923-9759-013_LTDutyStatementSr.PsychiatristSpecialistIGAHP12.16.24.pdf' target='_blank'>Duty Statement</a></strong>.</p>
                </p>
            
</div>

